Change: Regenerate the minified call sites of the Select2 fix and check them

Changing a source file under core/js, settings/js or apps/*/js without
regenerating its .min sibling ships the old code: the minified file is what a
deployment serves. The Select2 fix changed four call sites
(apps/files_external/js/settings.js, apps/systemtags/js/systemtagsfilelist.js,
core/js/systemtags/systemtagsinputfield.js, settings/js/settings.js); their
.min siblings are now regenerated with the pinned tools (terser 5.49.1,
clean-css-cli 5.6.3).

`make check-minified` regenerates the siblings and fails if anything changed,
leaving the regenerated files in the working tree because they are the result
that belongs in the commit. `make test-js-browser` depends on it. On main the
lint workflow already runs the same check on every push.
